From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcp90: Implement the money facets for the old msvcp versions.

Fast mode for msvcp60 .. msvcp90: the money facets were all spec stubs
(their ids and vtables commented out). money_base, _Mpunct and
moneypunct<T, false/true>, money_get and money_put, for char, wchar_t and
unsigned short, written from the C++ standard's descriptions:
moneypunct takes the locale's lconv (international or local symbol and
fraction digits, signs, grouping, separators) and builds pos_format and
neg_format from C99's cs_precedes, sep_by_space and sign_posn (_Makpat);
money_get reads by neg_format() (symbol optional unless showbase, the
first character of a sign, digits with separators and the fraction, the
rest of the sign after the value); money_put writes the digits with the
decimal point and grouping, the sign and symbol by the pattern, and pads to
the width (internal padding at the space or none field). The private
static helpers _Put, _Rep and _Putmfld stay stubs.
